# References Section — Required Format

Every substantive numbered note (`X.Y. Title.md`) ends with a `## References` section. When editing such a note, ensure this section exists and follows the exact format below.

## Format

```markdown
## References

- [Anthropic — Managed Agents Overview](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/overview)
- [MCP Specification](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification)
```

Rules:

- Heading is exactly `## References` (plural, capital R, level-2).
- One bullet per item: `- ` (hyphen + space), then `[Title](URL)`.
- Title is informative — prefer `Anthropic — Managed Agents Overview` to `Managed Agents Overview`. Use em-dash to attribute the source.
- **No bare URLs.** Always wrap in `[Title](URL)` form.
- **No annotations** after the link (no parenthetical descriptions). If commentary is needed, cite the reference inline in the body.

## Validation

When you are about to save edits to a numbered note, verify:

1. The note contains exactly one `## References` heading.
2. The heading is the last `##` heading in the file (References is the closing section).
3. Every item under it is a markdown link, not a bare URL.

If any reference URL was added in this turn and you did not actually verify it resolves, remove it. **Fabricated references are forbidden** — see `AGENTS.md` § 4.

## Source-of-truth skill

Detailed validation rules and a step-by-step normalization workflow live in [`.claude/skills/normalize-references/SKILL.md`](mdc:.claude/skills/normalize-references/SKILL.md). Follow that skill when asked to normalize, audit, or repair references.
